thub.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/a4759b3b3149d31169e00c77a7b019ab0e4d331a","node_id":"C_kwDOONu3BdoAKGE0NzU5YjNiMzE0OWQzMTE2OWUwMGM3N2E3YjAxOWFiMGU0ZDMzMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1","sha":"c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1"}],"sha":"a4759b3b3149d31169e00c77a7b019ab0e4d331a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/a4759b3b3149d31169e00c77a7b019ab0e4d331a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120506?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade","id":6120506,"login":"MetaGrenade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjA1MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T21:02:11Z","email":"fragzone.caleb@gmail.com","name":"Caleb Harrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T21:02:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"M0 - Foundations (#247)\n\n* Store support attachments privately and serve them through an authorized route\n\nSupport-ticket attachments were written to the public disk, so any file\nwas reachable by URL without authentication. Move them to a private disk\nand serve them from a controller that only lets the ticket owner and\nsupport staff download them.\n\n- SupportAttachmentStorage stores uploads on the private disk, records the\n  content-detected media type, sanitizes the display name and builds the\n  authorized download links; five controller code paths now use it\n- SupportAttachmentController streams downloads as attachments with\n  nosniff and no-store, and forces opaque binary for unsafe media types\n- web route (outside the support section toggle) and API route, with a\n  policy and OpenAPI documentation\n- migration and `support:attachments:privatize` command move existing\n  files off the public disk; both are idempotent and leave unmovable\n  rows untouched\n- fix SupportTicketMessage::ticket() and SupportTicketAudit::ticket(),\n  which looked for a nonexistent ticket_id column and always returned null\n- 13 new tests; existing tests updated for the private disk\n\n* Make search and text filters portable across MySQL, PostgreSQL and SQLite\n\n- Remove the unfinished mysql_fulltext search branches: they issued\n  MATCH ... AGAINST queries but no FULLTEXT index migrations exist, so\n  enabling them on MySQL would have errored\n- Search the three content types with case-insensitive whereLike and a\n  single relevance expression\n- Convert all 55 remaining `where(col, ''like'', ...)` filters to\n  whereLike/orWhereLike so admin filters and forum, blog, support and\n  shop searches behave the same on PostgreSQL (ILIKE) as on MySQL\n- Make the forum mention suggestion ordering case-insensitive\n\n* Run the test suite on MySQL 8 and PostgreSQL 16 in CI\n\n- Add ci-mysql and ci-pgsql jobs with real database services alongside\n  the existing SQLite job (kept as `ci` so required checks keep working)\n- Move the shared setup (PHP, Node, dependencies, env, asset build) into\n  a composite action\n- Give the blog status migration a PostgreSQL branch: Laravel''s enum()\n  is a varchar with a CHECK constraint there, which rejected the\n  ''scheduled'' status the migration introduces\n\n* ci: temporarily run tests on the M0 branch (remove before merge)\n\n* Use a single source for the app name and guard the CI database matrix\n\n- Home page SEO copy comes from config (seo.home.*) instead of hard-coded\n  starter-kit text; the document title already appends the site name\n- The logo reads the app name from the shared Inertia prop\n- Serve the web manifest from a controller so it carries the app name\n  (replaces the static public/site.webmanifest that said \"Laravel\")\n- Default APP_NAME is MetaForge in .env.example\n- Add a test that fails if a CI job meant to run on MySQL or PostgreSQL\n  is silently running on SQLite\n\n* Add release hygiene files, local services and an accurate README\n\n- SECURITY.md (GitHub private vulnerability reporting), security.txt,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, CHANGELOG.md, CODEOWNERS, Dependabot config, issue and\n  pull-request templates\n- compose.yaml with MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis, Mailpit and Meilisearch\n  (the last two behind profiles) for local development\n- README: name it MetaForge, state the pre-1.0 status and roadmap, list\n  the shop, polls and search modules, state the databases CI actually\n  tests (SQLite, MySQL 8, PostgreSQL 16) and document the private\n  support-attachment storage\n\n* Add static analysis, a secrets scan and a stability workflow\n\n- Larastan at level 5 over app, routes, factories and seeders, with a\n  baseline of the 604 existing findings so CI blocks any new one; the\n  baseline is the to-do list for raising the level. Mostly missing\n  relation return types and model docblocks.\n- gitleaks secrets scan and a weekly dependency-advisory audit\n- a scheduled workflow that repeats the suite in random order to surface\n  flaky or order-dependent tests with their seed (the one-off failure seen\n  earlier did not reproduce in 6 local runs across random orders and\n  timezones)\n- composer analyse and analyse:baseline scripts\n\n* Add the i18n infrastructure (English-only in 1.0)\n\nMake adding a language a translation task instead of a refactor, without\nextracting every string yet.\n\n- config/i18n.php: allow-list of supported languages and the translation\n  groups shared with the front end\n- SetLocale middleware: user preference, then cookie, then Accept-Language,\n  then the application default, restricted to the allow-list\n- Share locale, locales and flattened translations (with fallback to the\n  default language) as Inertia props, so they also work during SSR\n- useI18n() composable and lib/i18n helpers mirroring Laravel''s\n  placeholder and pluralisation syntax\n- `php artisan lang:check`, run in CI, fails if a language misses keys\n- convert the header navigation and buttons, skip link, footer and theme\n  menu to translation keys as the working example\n- docs/i18n.md describing the pieces and how to add strings and languages\n- tests for locale resolution, fallback, shared props and lang:check\n\n* ci: audit composer.lock directly in the scheduled advisories job\n\nWithout an install step, composer audit has no installed packages to inspect; --locked reads composer.lock instead.\n\n* Remove the temporary branch triggers and document APP_SUPPORTED_LOCALES\n\nThe workflows only need to run for pull requests and pushes to main and\ndevelop again now that M0 has been verified on its own branch. Also list\nthe supported-languages setting in .env.example.\n\n* Retry failed attachment moves and make the blog status rollback safe\n\nTwo review findings.\n\nAttachment move:\n- privatize() pointed the row at the private disk before deleting the\n  original and ignored delete() returning false, so a failed delete left a\n  publicly reachable copy that looked moved and was never retried. Now the\n  original is deleted first and the row only changes when that succeeds;\n  otherwise it stays on its original disk, the result is FAILED and the\n  command and migration report it loudly\n- an interrupted move (copied and deleted, row not yet updated) is now\n  completed on the next run instead of being reported missing\n\nBlog status migration:\n- down() restored the three-value status set while scheduled posts could\n  still exist, which PostgreSQL (CHECK constraint), MySQL strict mode and\n  SQLite all reject. Scheduled posts are returned to drafts first\n\nTests cover a failing delete and its retry, the interrupted move, and a\nreal rollback with a scheduled post; they fail against the previous code.\n\n* Fix the PostgreSQL blog status constraint for existing installations\n\nA migration that has already run is never run again, so adding the\nPostgreSQL branch to 2025_05_06_010000_update_blog_status_enum_for_scheduling\nonly helped fresh databases; existing PostgreSQL installations kept the\nthree-value CHECK constraint and still rejected ''scheduled''. The fresh-schema\nCI matrix could not show this.\n\n- add 2026_10_08_000100_allow_scheduled_blog_status_on_postgresql, which\n  replaces whichever CHECK constraint covers blogs.status with the\n  four-value one (idempotent, no-op on other databases); its down()\n  returns scheduled posts to drafts before narrowing the constraint\n- restore the 2025 migration''s PostgreSQL handling to what it was, keeping\n  only the scheduled-to-draft normalization in down() that MySQL strict\n  mode and SQLite need\n- add a PostgreSQL test that recreates an existing installation (legacy\n  constraint, scheduled rejected), runs the new migration, runs it again\n  and rolls it back with a scheduled post; plus a test that it does nothing\n  on other databases","tree":{"sha":"d5d1c2e32355f1c01b1b244871091e3e0b695ed9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/trees/d5d1c2e32355f1c01b1b244871091e3e0b695ed9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/commits/c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1","verification":{"payload":"tree d5d1c2e32355f1c01b1b244871091e3e0b695ed9\nparent ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e\nauthor Caleb Harrod <fragzone.caleb@gmail.com> 1791320531 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791320531 -0600\n\nM0 - Foundations (#247)\n\n* Store support attachments privately and serve them through an authorized route\n\nSupport-ticket attachments were written to the public disk, so any file\nwas reachable by URL without authentication. Move them to a private disk\nand serve them from a controller that only lets the ticket owner and\nsupport staff download them.\n\n- SupportAttachmentStorage stores uploads on the private disk, records the\n  content-detected media type, sanitizes the display name and builds the\n  authorized download links; five controller code paths now use it\n- SupportAttachmentController streams downloads as attachments with\n  nosniff and no-store, and forces opaque binary for unsafe media types\n- web route (outside the support section toggle) and API route, with a\n  policy and OpenAPI documentation\n- migration and `support:attachments:privatize` command move existing\n  files off the public disk; both are idempotent and leave unmovable\n  rows untouched\n- fix SupportTicketMessage::ticket() and SupportTicketAudit::ticket(),\n  which looked for a nonexistent ticket_id column and always returned null\n- 13 new tests; existing tests updated for the private disk\n\n* Make search and text filters portable across MySQL, PostgreSQL and SQLite\n\n- Remove the unfinished mysql_fulltext search branches: they issued\n  MATCH ... AGAINST queries but no FULLTEXT index migrations exist, so\n  enabling them on MySQL would have errored\n- Search the three content types with case-insensitive whereLike and a\n  single relevance expression\n- Convert all 55 remaining `where(col, ''like'', ...)` filters to\n  whereLike/orWhereLike so admin filters and forum, blog, support and\n  shop searches behave the same on PostgreSQL (ILIKE) as on MySQL\n- Make the forum mention suggestion ordering case-insensitive\n\n* Run the test suite on MySQL 8 and PostgreSQL 16 in CI\n\n- Add ci-mysql and ci-pgsql jobs with real database services alongside\n  the existing SQLite job (kept as `ci` so required checks keep working)\n- Move the shared setup (PHP, Node, dependencies, env, asset build) into\n  a composite action\n- Give the blog status migration a PostgreSQL branch: Laravel''s enum()\n  is a varchar with a CHECK constraint there, which rejected the\n  ''scheduled'' status the migration introduces\n\n* ci: temporarily run tests on the M0 branch (remove before merge)\n\n* Use a single source for the app name and guard the CI database matrix\n\n- Home page SEO copy comes from config (seo.home.*) instead of hard-coded\n  starter-kit text; the document title already appends the site name\n- The logo reads the app name from the shared Inertia prop\n- Serve the web manifest from a controller so it carries the app name\n  (replaces the static public/site.webmanifest that said \"Laravel\")\n- Default APP_NAME is MetaForge in .env.example\n- Add a test that fails if a CI job meant to run on MySQL or PostgreSQL\n  is silently running on SQLite\n\n* Add release hygiene files, local services and an accurate README\n\n- SECURITY.md (GitHub private vulnerability reporting), security.txt,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, CHANGELOG.md, CODEOWNERS, Dependabot config, issue and\n  pull-request templates\n- compose.yaml with MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis, Mailpit and Meilisearch\n  (the last two behind profiles) for local development\n- README: name it MetaForge, state the pre-1.0 status and roadmap, list\n  the shop, polls and search modules, state the databases CI actually\n  tests (SQLite, MySQL 8, PostgreSQL 16) and document the private\n  support-attachment storage\n\n* Add static analysis, a secrets scan and a stability workflow\n\n- Larastan at level 5 over app, routes, factories and seeders, with a\n  baseline of the 604 existing findings so CI blocks any new one; the\n  baseline is the to-do list for raising the level. Mostly missing\n  relation return types and model docblocks.\n- gitleaks secrets scan and a weekly dependency-advisory audit\n- a scheduled workflow that repeats the suite in random order to surface\n  flaky or order-dependent tests with their seed (the one-off failure seen\n  earlier did not reproduce in 6 local runs across random orders and\n  timezones)\n- composer analyse and analyse:baseline scripts\n\n* Add the i18n infrastructure (English-only in 1.0)\n\nMake adding a language a translation task instead of a refactor, without\nextracting every string yet.\n\n- config/i18n.php: allow-list of supported languages and the translation\n  groups shared with the front end\n- SetLocale middleware: user preference, then cookie, then Accept-Language,\n  then the application default, restricted to the allow-list\n- Share locale, locales and flattened translations (with fallback to the\n  default language) as Inertia props, so they also work during SSR\n- useI18n() composable and lib/i18n helpers mirroring Laravel''s\n  placeholder and pluralisation syntax\n- `php artisan lang:check`, run in CI, fails if a language misses keys\n- convert the header navigation and buttons, skip link, footer and theme\n  menu to translation keys as the working example\n- docs/i18n.md describing the pieces and how to add strings and languages\n- tests for locale resolution, fallback, shared props and lang:check\n\n* ci: audit composer.lock directly in the scheduled advisories job\n\nWithout an install step, composer audit has no installed packages to inspect; --locked reads composer.lock instead.\n\n* Remove the temporary branch triggers and document APP_SUPPORTED_LOCALES\n\nThe workflows only need to run for pull requests and pushes to main and\ndevelop again now that M0 has been verified on its own branch. Also list\nthe supported-languages setting in .env.example.\n\n* Retry failed attachment moves and make the blog status rollback safe\n\nTwo review findings.\n\nAttachment move:\n- privatize() pointed the row at the private disk before deleting the\n  original and ignored delete() returning false, so a failed delete left a\n  publicly reachable copy that looked moved and was never retried. Now the\n  original is deleted first and the row only changes when that succeeds;\n  otherwise it stays on its original disk, the result is FAILED and the\n  command and migration report it loudly\n- an interrupted move (copied and deleted, row not yet updated) is now\n  completed on the next run instead of being reported missing\n\nBlog status migration:\n- down() restored the three-value status set while scheduled posts could\n  still exist, which PostgreSQL (CHECK constraint), MySQL strict mode and\n  SQLite all reject. Scheduled posts are returned to drafts first\n\nTests cover a failing delete and its retry, the interrupted move, and a\nreal rollback with a scheduled post; they fail against the previous code.\n\n* Fix the PostgreSQL blog status constraint for existing installations\n\nA migration that has already run is never run again, so adding the\nPostgreSQL branch to 2025_05_06_010000_update_blog_status_enum_for_scheduling\nonly helped fresh databases; existing PostgreSQL installations kept the\nthree-value CHECK constraint and still rejected ''scheduled''. The fresh-schema\nCI matrix could not show this.\n\n- add 2026_10_08_000100_allow_scheduled_blog_status_on_postgresql, which\n  replaces whichever CHECK constraint covers blogs.status with the\n  four-value one (idempotent, no-op on other databases); its down()\n  returns scheduled posts to drafts before narrowing the constraint\n- restore the 2025 migration''s PostgreSQL handling to what it was, keeping\n  only the scheduled-to-draft normalization in down() that MySQL strict\n  mode and SQLite need\n- add a PostgreSQL test that recreates an existing installation (legacy\n  constraint, scheduled rejected), runs the new migration, runs it again\n  and rolls it back with a scheduled post; plus a test that it does nothing\n  on other databases","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxWHTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsc4QAIPNXUGd+cR/DF0OCnnSsZXR\nHfnVZgzsUKav8T3n7/nLiX9LegyUzKZQR0ZFtiNb45/7KcF/F6GOJ/Zix4UeYKww\n21XbnEWUjXDkVHA4i6srlOB/8Kxkgc/OAvXRuF5i2kAFOAaYaAaNHz4944roAKjq\nP7rqlfPyMYX3Pxz/Hso9H0o1oIUNN48JZXpDLw2jtEuu94IaiHj4rUzIj8UmhJLL\nli3tE1iT7g8APNKegMSOIcxyRVDn2lW9Tj61falcxsb4840W2MUs80lmQK7J0twO\nIQjYv8KHZPPoH2vy61Jmz8rF/4rzDoe2A9dkjF9QxE1/KwAXc00r8mCZG+gJZEZU\nAFh2cvECu1HC7zFOCo1emf0q9s++mtcLN1nL5EaAsyK2jsEb6G9yoBigyjplngen\ndCK2Qzllk6m7ZCgV2nYZ/PDXLmphNJ47xN9ItLyi2pUQfkDw1XFUX24wmYUsV+Zh\nHzVkBMcsHII4ohmvPSPvhLFm8sjS9A/xrYpuuHWhkd/XdM+FodTHFlzieN8s62Qt\nfdQwf+JS3Gsw2OWYJ4p9Gi7ck3RikF5HMQhL5dZSJEBuXpnPhqvEuZFZdFYhfZ1v\nlc5+fhjqvNAzpO6CX4eXhFhOA3jeijuw7o2OX457OUWJ+BuUxMWkcNGNJlp6z+6M\nKk6KTV2LIcllq1BJl9eb\n=sWR7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T21:02:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1","node_id":"C_kwDOONu3BdoAKGMyMjI0OGJiMGQ0N2ZmNjMzMzdkOWJmNDIwNTFhN2YyNzFjNjAwZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e","sha":"ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e"}],"sha":"c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/c22248bb0d47ff63337d9bf42051a7f271c600f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120506?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade","id":6120506,"login":"MetaGrenade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjA1MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:04:31Z","email":"fragzone.caleb@gmail.com","name":"Caleb Harrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:04:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Design Improvements - Backgrounds, Animations, Performance, Etc. (#246)\n\n* Add home page motion, an amber highlight colour and richer page backgrounds\n\n- Introduce a high-contrast amber `highlight` token (with button and badge\n  variants) as the partner to the indigo primary; used for the logo dot,\n  count badges, the active nav marker, the hero accents and the CTA\n- Add layered page backdrop (soft glows plus a fading grid) to every page\n  via the app shell and the auth layout, tuned separately for dark mode\n- Add grid, stripe, dot and gradient textures to the home page sections\n- Add CSS-only motion: staggered hero entrance, floating product preview,\n  growing chart bars, slow drifting glows and scroll-driven reveals; all\n  transform/opacity, no blur, and disabled for reduced-motion users\n\n* Redesign forum, blog and support pages on solid panels and cut scroll cost\n\n## Design\n- Give headers, toolbars, pagination bars, tables, lists and FAQ items on\n  the forum, blog, support, search and pricing pages an opaque card\n  background so text never sits on the page grid\n- Forum index: header card with a working thread search (replaces a\n  placeholder input), board rows with icons, tidier sidebar lists\n- Board and thread pages: carded header, pagination and thread table\n- Blog list: solid post cards with lazy-loaded covers, filters and\n  pagination on opaque panels\n- Support: header card, carded ticket toolbar and FAQ headings\n\n## Performance\n- Confine the page backdrop to a short, static, fading layer at the top\n  instead of four gradient layers over the whole document\n- Lazy-load and async-decode blog list images (featured stays eager)\n- Settle the looping hero animations after a few cycles, put scroll\n  reveals on containers instead of every card (18 -> 1 at load), and use\n  content-visibility on below-the-fold home sections\n- Drop the font stylistic-set features that added shaping work to all text\n\n* ﻿Replace the lone amber circle in the home CTA with a full-banner wash\n\nThe isolated amber blob in the corner looked out of place, and amber\nover the indigo gradient blended into a muddy mauve. Use a violet glow\nfrom the bottom right and a soft sheen from the top left instead, in\nlight and dark mode, and leave amber to the button so it remains the\nsingle high-contrast accent.\n\n* Replace the hero glow circles with edge-anchored washes that scale to any screen\n\nThe two fixed-size glow discs in the home hero read as isolated circles\non very wide screens. Swap them for percentage-sized radial washes\nanchored to the screen edges with an eased falloff, so they bleed off\nthe sides at any width. Apply the same treatment to the shared page\nbackdrop so every page matches, and remove the now-unused drift\nanimation.","tree":{"sha":"2f8847cac7337c583990cc3b458bdf331aafb1bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/trees/2f8847cac7337c583990cc3b458bdf331aafb1bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/commits/ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f8847cac7337c583990cc3b458bdf331aafb1bf\nparent 3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d\nauthor Caleb Harrod <fragzone.caleb@gmail.com> 1791313471 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313471 -0600\n\nDesign Improvements - Backgrounds, Animations, Performance, Etc. (#246)\n\n* Add home page motion, an amber highlight colour and richer page backgrounds\n\n- Introduce a high-contrast amber `highlight` token (with button and badge\n  variants) as the partner to the indigo primary; used for the logo dot,\n  count badges, the active nav marker, the hero accents and the CTA\n- Add layered page backdrop (soft glows plus a fading grid) to every page\n  via the app shell and the auth layout, tuned separately for dark mode\n- Add grid, stripe, dot and gradient textures to the home page sections\n- Add CSS-only motion: staggered hero entrance, floating product preview,\n  growing chart bars, slow drifting glows and scroll-driven reveals; all\n  transform/opacity, no blur, and disabled for reduced-motion users\n\n* Redesign forum, blog and support pages on solid panels and cut scroll cost\n\n## Design\n- Give headers, toolbars, pagination bars, tables, lists and FAQ items on\n  the forum, blog, support, search and pricing pages an opaque card\n  background so text never sits on the page grid\n- Forum index: header card with a working thread search (replaces a\n  placeholder input), board rows with icons, tidier sidebar lists\n- Board and thread pages: carded header, pagination and thread table\n- Blog list: solid post cards with lazy-loaded covers, filters and\n  pagination on opaque panels\n- Support: header card, carded ticket toolbar and FAQ headings\n\n## Performance\n- Confine the page backdrop to a short, static, fading layer at the top\n  instead of four gradient layers over the whole document\n- Lazy-load and async-decode blog list images (featured stays eager)\n- Settle the looping hero animations after a few cycles, put scroll\n  reveals on containers instead of every card (18 -> 1 at load), and use\n  content-visibility on below-the-fold home sections\n- Drop the font stylistic-set features that added shaping work to all text\n\n* ﻿Replace the lone amber circle in the home CTA with a full-banner wash\n\nThe isolated amber blob in the corner looked out of place, and amber\nover the indigo gradient blended into a muddy mauve. Use a violet glow\nfrom the bottom right and a soft sheen from the top left instead, in\nlight and dark mode, and leave amber to the button so it remains the\nsingle high-contrast accent.\n\n* Replace the hero glow circles with edge-anchored washes that scale to any screen\n\nThe two fixed-size glow discs in the home hero read as isolated circles\non very wide screens. Swap them for percentage-sized radial washes\nanchored to the screen edges with an eased falloff, so they bleed off\nthe sides at any width. Apply the same treatment to the shared page\nbackdrop so every page matches, and remove the now-unused drift\nanimation.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUZACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcoQQAEc4UPoZG5BmUKzNqjyovu83\nfzUilh7e2WwV9x3BVM47eQhzqus7ILXS4jauz0IBK9U4zHg8t4+128KQYOXz02u4\nG1eePrFRTvILGDqhwm8bmIKi8PXnKUeJxrfnNVwFyjzC9r9WIgKd0YHv8LQ7IHlj\n8y4aeCOhlzm9X5KtJco8IoDEc/il7lOv7TGBEcj5JJ1RbSOdiGTwT3GDgrGS43y5\nc1sVO1llrslcaBQzVeeoX55AmoPyaXpj2sczJ0NOz9Fm6ndRF6XCmxI7Ooj6fuM2\nvYdYMVlDWuKE/ISEQnqqmaDYvdHvdz3Y03GPiWGi9Wu0fgrupFdzh191kQGEPeTQ\nAXdb7+pw1HIpEoVYdbcvPZ6DiRQzz31xt5RAwGNp8WX+9AHPek6P4y7zFJofpJsg\ndfxsxjJHWTdTRiMDAq5KVwyu2O6keg5Av/l2ruWrwoeuXJxvMWwynhv2kv1GdB9a\nFDSaZBZvuzfhoeWKMX2wEgtnuXs3R4B2bum6NsCA80TgoXQ6yFMXm+32eqPV8slX\nU44+M986XMkKNH9HOAeG7lWu5oP9K9w+KhzQwPga1bJn5E8otBpp9DGJN5b2JIqu\nEAamzwK6kk6P/m6oPkcSbv4ar9I7z9+Riem0+Fto70iRGDEeAAYqSR5pwlDqSyZI\nnk15Ut4LBioFtHkM+1QA\n=xHd6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T19:04:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e","node_id":"C_kwDOONu3BdoAKGZmOTQ5YzA1ZjE5MGE4ZjA2NWVjNmJhMmQwNWZiNDViZDQwZjk0MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d","sha":"3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d"}],"sha":"ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/ff949c05f190a8f065ec6ba2d05fb45bd40f940e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120506?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade","id":6120506,"login":"MetaGrenade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjA1MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:05:21Z","email":"fragzone.caleb@gmail.com","name":"Caleb Harrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:05:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Modernize the design system, layouts and pages with light/dark themes (#245)\n\n* Modernize the design system, layouts and pages with light/dark themes\n\n- Rebuild design tokens: zinc neutrals with a single indigo brand colour,\n  semantic success/warning/info tokens, surface canvas, Inter font\n- Shared appearance state with a header/footer theme toggle, themed\n  toasts and Stripe Elements\n- Sticky opaque header with active nav, search trigger and guest\n  sign-in buttons; new site footer and skip link\n- Grouped, sticky navigation for the admin panel and settings, with\n  scrollable tabs on mobile; refreshed auth layout\n- Rewrite the landing and pricing pages without autoplay carousels\n- Replace hard-coded greys and status colours across pages with theme\n  tokens so dark mode renders correctly\n- Fix the logo icon ignoring its size, the header layout rendering as a\n  sidebar shell, and pagination/forum rows overflowing on phones\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix appearance hydration, live Stripe theming and checkout labels\n\n- Keep the shared appearance state at its server-rendered defaults until\n  after hydration; the <html> theme class is still applied immediately,\n  so there is no flash and no hydration mismatch on /settings/appearance\n- Re-apply the Stripe Elements appearance when the resolved theme\n  changes (toggle or system preference) on Pricing, Billing and\n  Payment Methods\n- Replace mojibake ellipses in the Pricing checkout status labels","tree":{"sha":"2effea27798417f036780642ff05cc6b44c51abd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/trees/2effea27798417f036780642ff05cc6b44c51abd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/commits/3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2effea27798417f036780642ff05cc6b44c51abd\nparent 108d2d2fa8115ef3562651623ffbe96d4402daf0\nauthor Caleb Harrod <fragzone.caleb@gmail.com> 1791288321 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791288321 -0600\n\nModernize the design system, layouts and pages with light/dark themes (#245)\n\n* Modernize the design system, layouts and pages with light/dark themes\n\n- Rebuild design tokens: zinc neutrals with a single indigo brand colour,\n  semantic success/warning/info tokens, surface canvas, Inter font\n- Shared appearance state with a header/footer theme toggle, themed\n  toasts and Stripe Elements\n- Sticky opaque header with active nav, search trigger and guest\n  sign-in buttons; new site footer and skip link\n- Grouped, sticky navigation for the admin panel and settings, with\n  scrollable tabs on mobile; refreshed auth layout\n- Rewrite the landing and pricing pages without autoplay carousels\n- Replace hard-coded greys and status colours across pages with theme\n  tokens so dark mode renders correctly\n- Fix the logo icon ignoring its size, the header layout rendering as a\n  sidebar shell, and pagination/forum rows overflowing on phones\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix appearance hydration, live Stripe theming and checkout labels\n\n- Keep the shared appearance state at its server-rendered defaults until\n  after hydration; the <html> theme class is still applied immediately,\n  so there is no flash and no hydration mismatch on /settings/appearance\n- Re-apply the Stripe Elements appearance when the resolved theme\n  changes (toggle or system preference) on Pricing, Billing and\n  Payment Methods\n- Replace mojibake ellipses in the Pricing checkout status labels","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxOQBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqj8QAGLd9UNrVdK61J0CawYmY/to\nXTGvYYll/c8PXrIqjAR9ouK7+NpSon4I22WSpTz9HfK7balbuXrXiVnORLmtDHaw\nIlRfsc4e1P0KsQnxOZBCO/dFhofqKejJTfo0MbdSyXKkqOlixpN4wivdreYzLqkC\naJPaU7Dp2Gr8n7gL8fNa3vUJpxl5qNkwIFYByNhaGVt0b+uVBX96kjnTbXIr4NKW\n66uUHCHDAjsNdz5DhFJGxM/xZ6NzsIAkbCvggWGAy/iapsmRU3py+BiLLbPu9Jgp\nfy1HHwnX/l8yt7n5hp5Mqk2TztDGRu+RHpvTYovPQ08H09Y9uuRgwTVwXp8J67af\n8epgOhh/zTUa0w5RhrGKQGk7RTFVdDfgmuOmv0qmxQFTMt84D9Dr0vGu7Iulr5sj\nJ719c7sYpnAFHnFQGN2TIZ0CNkQAryBB0BUEhyEOrCkiBczga//oxGATq5cFkw42\nmg3HjX5eZcXeF8UrhPuUeub/TbWhwl90W+p3Euv8E6E2+8R77fMnPm2cjCT4/jig\nG/nVZntzk55CnrPZpiNwFTotZVrLgpSIbWSb4ptnsPgJCodEpdX9Z/O1U+hkRk6v\nc3dXj9KnbVn1HFvrnLA00zBrMbosWoy4Jwr5CYra4xBC7YZRiU08o7yCdVCa2jzV\nk6cWH56EGAVqN2TNaB4S\n=sIRh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:05:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d","node_id":"C_kwDOONu3BdoAKDNmZjJkZGMyODA4OTViNWEyNmI3OTgxYjc3NjVjZWQxZmY2YjVhNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commit/108d2d2fa8115ef3562651623ffbe96d4402daf0","sha":"108d2d2fa8115ef3562651623ffbe96d4402daf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/108d2d2fa8115ef3562651623ffbe96d4402daf0"}],"sha":"3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/3ff2ddc280895b5a26b7981b7765ced1ff6b5a4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120506?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MetaGrenade","id":6120506,"login":"MetaGrenade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjA1MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MetaGrenade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/commits/108d2d2fa8115ef3562651623ffbe96d4402daf0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:40:06Z","email":"fragzone.caleb@gmail.com","name":"Caleb Harrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:40:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade to Laravel 13 + modern front-end stack; security, SEO and bug fixes (#244)\n\n* Upgrade to Laravel 13 and latest backend packages\n\n- laravel/framework ^13, inertia-laravel ^3, cashier ^16, permission ^8,\n  tinker ^3, phpunit ^12; PHP requirement raised to ^8.3\n- Sync config files with the Laravel 13 skeleton, including JSON session\n  serialization and an explicit cache serializable-class allow-list\n- Republish Inertia v3 config and add Cashier 16 subscription item\n  meter columns\n- Use PreventRequestForgery in place of the deprecated VerifyCsrfToken\n- Run PreventBannedUser after StartSession so session-authenticated\n  banned users are actually logged out\n- Stop calling the Stripe API when handling customer.subscription.deleted\n  (the subscription no longer exists there), which caused 500s and\n  endless webhook retries\n- Convert @test annotations to attributes for PHPUnit 12; remove unused\n  Pest bootstrap; fix tsconfig referencing missing vue/tsx types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove unused Icon component that imported every Lucide icon\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix stored XSS in forum posts and blog bodies\n\nForum threads/replies (web and API) and blog bodies were stored as raw\nHTML and rendered with v-html, so any member could run script in other\nusers'' (including admins'') sessions.\n\n- Add an HtmlSanitizer (symfony/html-sanitizer) with a strict ''forum''\n  policy matching the editor''s output and a richer ''article'' policy for\n  staff-written posts\n- Apply it via a SanitizedHtml Eloquent cast on ForumPost, Blog and their\n  revision models so every write path is covered, and in the forum\n  controllers before the empty-body check\n- Add a content:sanitize command to clean previously stored records\n- Require PHP ^8.4, matching the Symfony 8 components Laravel 13\n  resolves to\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade front-end to Vite 8, Inertia 3, Tailwind 4, Tiptap 3\n\n- Vite 8 (Rolldown), laravel-vite-plugin 3 with self-hosted fonts,\n  @inertiajs/vite for page resolution and the SSR dev server\n- Inertia 3: withApp/serverHead entry points, typed shared props\n- Tailwind 4 via @tailwindcss/vite; CSS-first theme, tw-animate-css\n- Regenerate shadcn-vue components on reka-ui and drop radix-vue;\n  migrate Checkbox/Switch bindings to v-model/model-value (fixes ACP\n  switches that never bound with v-model:checked)\n- Tiptap 3 StarterKit, Lucide via @lucide/vue, Echo 2, vue-sonner 2,\n  VueUse, TypeScript 6, ESLint 10\n- Revert ''outline'' variant literals the Tailwind upgrade tool wrongly\n  renamed to ''outline-solid''\n- Fix router.delete() calls that passed data as a third argument, which\n  dropped onFinish/preserveScroll and left buttons stuck loading\n- Fix TrustSafety pagination reading unwrapped refs in the template\n- Register dayjs plugins centrally (PollEdit relied on load order)\n- Real-time notifications subscribed to private-private-App.Models.User\n  and always failed auth; load Echo/Pusher lazily and refresh auth\n  headers per request; treat empty PUSHER_* env values as unset\n- Prefer the XSRF cookie over the stale csrf meta tag for fetch()\n  requests, avoiding 419s after login without a reload\n- Show session flash messages as toasts globally (most ACP actions had\n  no visible feedback) and theme the toaster\n- Editor/content CSS: fix word-break mid-word, light-mode table colours\n  and an invisible placeholder\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add SEO foundation, sitemap and robots; stop leaking admin routes\n\nSEO\n- Seo service: per-page title, description, canonical, Open Graph,\n  Twitter and robots tags plus JSON-LD, rendered server-side for\n  crawlers and kept in sync client-side via Inertia''s serverHead\n- Structured data for the home page (WebSite/SearchAction,\n  Organization), blog posts (BlogPosting, BreadcrumbList), forum threads\n  (DiscussionForumPosting) and products (Product)\n- Private and low-value routes are noindex; SEO_INDEXING disables\n  indexing site-wide (default: production only)\n- Dynamic /sitemap.xml (cached, respects enabled website sections) and\n  /robots.txt; RSS autodiscovery, favicon.svg and web manifest\n\nSecurity / performance\n- Ziggy route groups: guests and members no longer receive the ~160\n  admin route definitions; the full route map is no longer serialised\n  into every Inertia response (only on SSR-rendered initial loads)\n- Shared props (notifications, quote) are now lazily evaluated\n- ziggy.location includes the query string so filters are restored\n- Inactive products are no longer viewable by URL\n\nFixes\n- ACP dashboard used MySQL-only DATE_FORMAT and 500''d on SQLite/Postgres;\n  add a driver-aware Sql::yearMonth() helper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden security defaults and update CI\n\n- Named rate limiters for registration, password reset, password\n  confirmation, two-factor challenges (previously unthrottled and\n  brute-forceable), forum/support posting, reports, search and billing\n- SecurityHeaders middleware: nosniff, frame, referrer, permissions and\n  COOP headers, HSTS over HTTPS, and a nonce-based Content Security\n  Policy (configurable in config/security.php, report-only supported)\n- Production defaults: stricter Password::defaults(), prohibit\n  destructive DB commands, optional URL::forceHttps(); N+1 lazy-loading\n  warnings logged in local development; Vite asset prefetching\n- Only write users.last_activity_at once a minute and without touching\n  updated_at, instead of on every request\n- CI: actions v7, Node from .nvmrc, Composer cache, dependency audits,\n  and enforce Pint/Prettier/ESLint instead of silently fixing\n- Document new settings in .env.example\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix front-end bugs found by type-checking and layout testing; enforce types in CI\n\nType errors: 172 -> 0, and vue-tsc now runs in CI. Many of the errors\nwere real bugs:\n- Billing invoice/webhook and forum report pagination never worked\n  (reka Pagination rendered without total, disabling its own buttons)\n- Search results pagination bound v-model to a nested ref, replacing it\n  with a number so page changes never navigated; defaultPerPage given a\n  ComputedRef produced NaN\n- Saving SLA settings threw (form.setDefaults does not exist)\n- Closing the assignment-rule delete dialog threw (.value on an\n  unwrapped ref in the template)\n- Filter selects passed the DOM Event as filter overrides, leaking\n  isTrusted into the query string\n- Checkbox handlers treated ''indeterminate'' as checked\n- Alert ''warning''/''success'' and Button ''success'' variants were used but\n  undefined; add them\n- Ticket and FAQ deletion in the ACP now require confirmation\n\nLayout / responsiveness:\n- ACP pages overflowed by 600-1000px on phones (and /acp/support on\n  desktop): constrain the content column so tables scroll in place\n- Fix overflow in the home carousel, blog share buttons, forum board and\n  thread headers, and the support ticket toolbar at tablet/phone widths\n- Unovis charts collapsed to 300px wide; stretch the chart container\n- Allow same-origin frames in the CSP; Echo/Pusher types, shallowRef\n  editor instance, typed shared props and template globals\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply Pint and Prettier across the codebase\n\nFormatting only, no behaviour changes. CI now enforces both instead of\nsilently fixing, so the codebase needs to start from a clean baseline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Refresh the Ziggy route map when the user''s route group changes\n\n@routes only renders on full page loads, so a staff member who signed in\nfrom the guest login page (an Inertia visit) kept the public route map\nand ACP pages failed with Ziggy''s \"route is not in the route list\"\nuntil a reload. Signing out had the reverse problem, leaving admin\nroutes in the browser.\n\nThe client now reports the route group it holds in an X-Ziggy-Group\nheader on every Inertia request, and the server includes the route map\nin the ziggy prop only when that differs from the user''s current group.\nThe client swaps the new map into Ziggy''s config on success, so no\nreload is needed and the post-login flash toast is preserved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Create fonts-manifest.dev.json\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f17845e7566ec9bb693dd46136ed84a969e424ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/trees/f17845e7566ec9bb693dd46136ed84a969e424ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MetaGrenade/laravel-vue/git/commits/108d2d2fa8115ef3562651623ffbe96d4402daf0","verification":{"payload":"tree f17845e7566ec9bb693dd46136ed84a969e424ee\nparent 7cd08eb4f7c8e387fcac8124a28702bf162b0659\nauthor Caleb Harrod <fragzone.caleb@gmail.com> 1791254406 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791254406 -0600\n\nUpgrade to Laravel 13 + modern front-end stack; security, SEO and bug fixes (#244)\n\n* Upgrade to Laravel 13 and latest backend packages\n\n- laravel/framework ^13, inertia-laravel ^3, cashier ^16, permission ^8,\n  tinker ^3, phpunit ^12; PHP requirement raised to ^8.3\n- Sync config files with the Laravel 13 skeleton, including JSON session\n  serialization and an explicit cache serializable-class allow-list\n- Republish Inertia v3 config and add Cashier 16 subscription item\n  meter columns\n- Use PreventRequestForgery in place of the deprecated VerifyCsrfToken\n- Run PreventBannedUser after StartSession so session-authenticated\n  banned users are actually logged out\n- Stop calling the Stripe API when handling customer.subscription.deleted\n  (the subscription no longer exists there), which caused 500s and\n  endless webhook retries\n- Convert @test annotations to attributes for PHPUnit 12; remove unused\n  Pest bootstrap; fix tsconfig referencing missing vue/tsx types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove unused Icon component that imported every Lucide icon\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix stored XSS in forum posts and blog bodies\n\nForum threads/replies (web and API) and blog bodies were stored as raw\nHTML and rendered with v-html, so any member could run script in other\nusers'' (including admins'') sessions.\n\n- Add an HtmlSanitizer (symfony/html-sanitizer) with a strict ''forum''\n  policy matching the editor''s output and a richer ''article'' policy for\n  staff-written posts\n- Apply it via a SanitizedHtml Eloquent cast on ForumPost, Blog and their\n  revision models so every write path is covered, and in the forum\n  controllers before the empty-body check\n- Add a content:sanitize command to clean previously stored records\n- Require PHP ^8.4, matching the Symfony 8 components Laravel 13\n  resolves to\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade front-end to Vite 8, Inertia 3, Tailwind 4, Tiptap 3\n\n- Vite 8 (Rolldown), laravel-vite-plugin 3 with self-hosted fonts,\n  @inertiajs/vite for page resolution and the SSR dev server\n- Inertia 3: withApp/serverHead entry points, typed shared props\n- Tailwind 4 via @tailwindcss/vite; CSS-first theme, tw-animate-css\n- Regenerate shadcn-vue components on reka-ui and drop radix-vue;\n  migrate Checkbox/Switch bindings to v-model/model-value (fixes ACP\n  switches that never bound with v-model:checked)\n- Tiptap 3 StarterKit, Lucide via @lucide/vue, Echo 2, vue-sonner 2,\n  VueUse, TypeScript 6, ESLint 10\n- Revert ''outline'' variant literals the Tailwind upgrade tool wrongly\n  renamed to ''outline-solid''\n- Fix router.delete() calls that passed data as a third argument, which\n  dropped onFinish/preserveScroll and left buttons stuck loading\n- Fix TrustSafety pagination reading unwrapped refs in the template\n- Register dayjs plugins centrally (PollEdit relied on load order)\n- Real-time notifications subscribed to private-private-App.Models.User\n  and always failed auth; load Echo/Pusher lazily and refresh auth\n  headers per request; treat empty PUSHER_* env values as unset\n- Prefer the XSRF cookie over the stale csrf meta tag for fetch()\n  requests, avoiding 419s after login without a reload\n- Show session flash messages as toasts globally (most ACP actions had\n  no visible feedback) and theme the toaster\n- Editor/content CSS: fix word-break mid-word, light-mode table colours\n  and an invisible placeholder\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add SEO foundation, sitemap and robots; stop leaking admin routes\n\nSEO\n- Seo service: per-page title, description, canonical, Open Graph,\n  Twitter and robots tags plus JSON-LD, rendered server-side for\n  crawlers and kept in sync client-side via Inertia''s serverHead\n- Structured data for the home page (WebSite/SearchAction,\n  Organization), blog posts (BlogPosting, BreadcrumbList), forum threads\n  (DiscussionForumPosting) and products (Product)\n- Private and low-value routes are noindex; SEO_INDEXING disables\n  indexing site-wide (default: production only)\n- Dynamic /sitemap.xml (cached, respects enabled website sections) and\n  /robots.txt; RSS autodiscovery, favicon.svg and web manifest\n\nSecurity / performance\n- Ziggy route groups: guests and members no longer receive the ~160\n  admin route definitions; the full route map is no longer serialised\n  into every Inertia response (only on SSR-rendered initial loads)\n- Shared props (notifications, quote) are now lazily evaluated\n- ziggy.location includes the query string so filters are restored\n- Inactive products are no longer viewable by URL\n\nFixes\n- ACP dashboard used MySQL-only DATE_FORMAT and 500''d on SQLite/Postgres;\n  add a driver-aware Sql::yearMonth() helper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden security defaults and update CI\n\n- Named rate limiters for registration, password reset, password\n  confirmation, two-factor challenges (previously unthrottled and\n  brute-forceable), forum/support posting, reports, search and billing\n- SecurityHeaders middleware: nosniff, frame, referrer, permissions and\n  COOP headers, HSTS over HTTPS, and a nonce-based Content Security\n  Policy (configurable in config/security.php, report-only supported)\n- Production defaults: stricter Password::defaults(), prohibit\n  destructive DB commands, optional URL::forceHttps(); N+1 lazy-loading\n  warnings logged in local development; Vite asset prefetching\n- Only write users.last_activity_at once a minute and without touching\n  updated_at, instead of on every request\n- CI: actions v7, Node from .nvmrc, Composer cache, dependency audits,\n  and enforce Pint/Prettier/ESLint instead of silently fixing\n- Document new settings in .env.example\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix front-end bugs found by type-checking and layout testing; enforce types in CI\n\nType errors: 172 -> 0, and vue-tsc now runs in CI. Many of the errors\nwere real bugs:\n- Billing invoice/webhook and forum report pagination never worked\n  (reka Pagination rendered without total, disabling its own buttons)\n- Search results pagination bound v-model to a nested ref, replacing it\n  with a number so page changes never navigated; defaultPerPage given a\n  ComputedRef produced NaN\n- Saving SLA settings threw (form.setDefaults does not exist)\n- Closing the assignment-rule delete dialog threw (.value on an\n  unwrapped ref in the template)\n- Filter selects passed the DOM Event as filter overrides, leaking\n  isTrusted into the query string\n- Checkbox handlers treated ''indeterminate'' as checked\n- Alert ''warning''/''success'' and Button ''success'' variants were used but\n  undefined; add them\n- Ticket and FAQ deletion in the ACP now require confirmation\n\nLayout / responsiveness:\n- ACP pages overflowed by 600-1000px on phones (and /acp/support on\n  desktop): constrain the content column so tables scroll in place\n- Fix overflow in the home carousel, blog share buttons, forum board and\n  thread headers, and the support ticket toolbar at tablet/phone widths\n- Unovis charts collapsed to 300px wide; stretch the chart container\n- Allow same-origin frames in the CSP; Echo/Pusher types, shallowRef\n  editor instance, typed shared props and template globals\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply Pint and Prettier across the codebase\n\nFormatting only, no behaviour changes. CI now enforces both instead of\nsilently fixing, so the codebase needs to start from a clean baseline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Refresh the Ziggy route map when the user''s route group changes\n\n@routes only renders on full page loads, so a staff member who signed in\nfrom the guest login page (an Inertia visit) kept the public route map\nand ACP pages failed with Ziggy''s \"route is not in the route list\"\nuntil a reload. Signing out had the reverse problem, leaving admin\nroutes in the browser.\n\nThe client now reports the route group it holds in an X-Ziggy-Group\nheader on every Inertia request, and the server includes the route map\nin the ziggy prop only when that differs from the user''s current group.\nThe client swaps the new map into Ziggy''s config on success, so no\nreload is needed and the post-login flash toast is preserved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Create fonts-manifest.dev.json\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxF+GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiS0QAK9gvpxw6CL7IZM6PBNFCBvD\nyISN62Xr94cMvxqSy2HZ5BS8ayvi8U+XGadqN7Ae2B0Rtd3wMTgZwGUWi0DvZG2A\nKA/BkNdLTjCgYzql3Hb+3Nf/tTAubjyRG04Z4/o06VLiipO1itz3EI5kg5WWItbU\nD8